From: CSouffargi <cs@karo-electronics.de>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: imx: src: fix imx_src_is_m4_enabled redefinition on
 32-bit i.MX

The header guards the real prototype with CONFIG_SOC_IMX8M, but
arch/arm/mach-imx/src.c also provides the function whenever
CONFIG_HAVE_IMX_SRC is set (i.MX5/6/7, 32-bit). Building for i.MX6ULL
then hits a redefinition between the static inline stub and the real
definition. Align the guard with the condition that actually builds
src.c (obj-$(CONFIG_HAVE_IMX_SRC) += src.o) so declaration and
definition can never diverge, on any platform.

Signed-off-by: CSouffargi <cs@karo-electronics.de>
---
 include/soc/imx/src.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/soc/imx/src.h b/include/soc/imx/src.h
--- a/include/soc/imx/src.h
+++ b/include/soc/imx/src.h
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 #ifndef __SOC_IMX_SRC_H
 #define __SOC_IMX_SRC_H
 
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SOC_IMX8M)
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_IMX_SRC)
 bool imx_src_is_m4_enabled(void);
 #else
 static inline bool imx_src_is_m4_enabled(void) { return false; }
